 "summary": {
  "text": "Reporting that Trump directed federal agencies to call Lake Ontario \"Lake America\" has drawn only scattered Democratic comment. @tedlieu flagged it Aug 28 in flat disbelief, drawing two member retweets, with single retweets Aug 29 and Sept 2 and then no posts for nearly a week. On Sept 7 @Rep_Stansbury posted a Labor Day message insisting New Mexico will not change its name — adjacent rather than clearly about the lake — and on Sept 8 @FrankPallone mocked \"another futile attempt to rename a place that didn't vote for him.\" Framing moved from astonishment to state-pride defiance to ridicule. Evidence stays thin: three posts, three members, one each, nothing new since Sept 8. Open: whether the directive is formal or…",
